  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Machado delivered the go-ahead three-run homer in the tenth after Castellanos tied it in the ninth.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't wait for clean wins. They came into the tenth still down, Castellanos leveled it with one swing, and Machado finished what he had started. Five RBIs on the night, the difference between another loss and staying afloat. The bullpen held when it had to: Hart kept it scoreless early, Morejon threw two clean frames, Miller closed without drama. Walker Buehler threw five strong innings and left with a lead; the team lost it in one inning against Texas, then recaptured it when it mattered. This is how fragile teams win close games. They don't get one chance, they scrape together chances until one lands.",
    "what_to_watch": "Nathan Eovaldi starts tonight at 11:35 AM Pacific, and he's been giving up 4.23 per nine this season. Vulnerable but not broken. The Padres get a day game after an extra-inning grind; momentum is a word, but three straight one-run wins is arithmetic, and that math gets harder.",
